UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 2019 in Laramie, Wyoming, Bond''s Brewing Company began as a passion project to craft unique, high-quality beer and foster a welcoming community space. From the start, the brewery focused on developing its own distinct recipes, aiming to reflect a dedication to craftsmanship and flavor in every pint.

The company produces a lineup of standard beers available year-round across its two Wyoming taprooms in Laramie and Buffalo, along with seasonal offerings. Its portfolio includes styles such as a red ale, fruited wheat ale, kolsch, Scottish ale, and hop-forward pale ale, all brewed with ingredients like specialty malts, Yakima Valley hops, and fresh fruit. In 2023, the Buffalo location expanded the concept by adding a craft cocktail program made with high-quality ingredients, including house-made mixes such as a clam-juice Michelada and a pickle-juice variant. The brewery operates as both a production facility and a hospitality venue, though specific facility size, headcount, and annual volume are not disclosed.

Bond''s Brewing serves locals and visitors seeking a community-oriented craft beverage experience. Its beers and cocktails are sold directly through its taprooms, and the company collaborates with other small businesses for events and partnerships. The brand positions itself within Wyoming''s growing craft beverage scene, targeting craft beer enthusiasts, tourists, and residents looking for a gathering place.

The company states that community is at the core of its mission, viewing beer as an experience that brings people together. It emphasizes innovation, quality, and a commitment to contributing to the vibrant culture of Wyoming. The addition of cocktails in Buffalo reflects a desire to offer guests more options while maintaining the same creative standards applied to its beer.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Craft beer brewing", "Seasonal beer production", "Fruit-infused brewing", "Hop-forward brewing", "Cocktail preparation", "Taproom operation", "Community event hosting", "Collaboration with local businesses"], "industries": ["Craft beverage", "Hospitality", "Tourism"], "materials": ["Malted barley (crystal, specialty, pilsner, European malts)", "Hops (Yakima Valley)", "Fresh fruit (rhubarb, raspberries, strawberries, mango)", "Coriander", "Lemon peel", "Clam juice", "Tomatoes", "Spices", "Pickle juice"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Award-winning beer", "Craft cocktails made with high-quality ingredients", "Community-focused gathering place", "Unique recipes developed in-house", "Year-round standard beer lineup"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2019 in Laramie, Wyoming -> /about", "Expanded to Buffalo in 2023 -> /about", "Produces standard beers year-round -> /services", "Offers craft cocktails at Buffalo location -> /about", "Operates two taprooms in Laramie and Buffalo -> /about", "Beer varieties include Arrowhead Red, Rhuberry, Mango Michelada, BEER (Kolsch), Highlander Scottish Ale, Michelada, 2nd Street Wheat, Citra-Hop-A-Dopolis, PICKELADA -> /services", "Community-focused mission -> /about", "Award-winning beer mentioned -> /about", "Ingredients include specialty malts, Yakima Valley hops, fresh fruit -> /services", "Headquarters in Buffalo, Wyoming -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Founded in 2019 in the heart of Laramie, Wyoming, Bond''s Brewing Company was built on a passion for crafting unique, high-quality beer and fostering a welcoming community space.", "founded_year": "2019", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bond-s-brewing-company-buffalo' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BorgWarner Inc. is headquartered in Hanover Park, Illinois. The company designs and manufactures systems for industrial and automotive applications, applying deep engineering expertise and advanced manufacturing capabilities to deliver solutions tailored to evolving industrial performance requirements.

Its product portfolio centers on battery energy storage systems (BESS), including generator battery systems, uninterruptible power supply units, and turbine generator systems. The company operates a production and service footprint across North America and Europe, with over 5 GWh of production capacity supported by a global supply base for cells and components. Core processes encompass full mechanical, electrical, testing, and validation capabilities, engineering services, and remanufacturing to extend product life. A removable electronics unit (RCB) enables easy service and repair.

BorgWarner serves industrial energy storage markets, providing stationary energy storage based on high-energy NMC battery technology for grid interaction and energy optimization. Customers deploy modular platforms ranging from rack-level backup to multi-megawatt-hour installations, addressing needs from seconds to hours of discharge duration.

The company differentiates itself through a cell-agnostic hardware and software architecture, automotive-grade battery management with redundant safety architecture, and a common hardware foundation that enables rapid deployment across power and energy scales.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Mechanical, electrical, testing, and validation", "Engineering services", "Remanufacturing", "Removable electronics unit (RCB) service and repair", "Battery energy storage system (BESS) manufacturing", "Generator battery system manufacturing", "Uninterruptible power supply (UPS) manufacturing", "Turbine generator system manufacturing", "Cell-agnostic hardware and software platform development", "Automotive-grade battery management system integration"], "industries": ["Industrial energy storage", "Grid interaction and energy optimization", "Stationary energy storage", "Battery energy storage systems (BESS)", "Uninterruptible power supply (UPS)", "Generator battery systems", "Turbine generator systems"], "materials": ["NMC battery cells"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Over 5 GWh production capacity", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 5 GWh production capacity", "Cell-agnostic hardware and software architecture", "Automotive-grade battery technology with redundant safety architecture", "Production and service footprint in North America and Europe", "Remanufacturing to extend product life"], "facts_used": ["HQ: Hanover Park, Illinois -> db", "Designs and manufactures systems -> page ''/''", "Industrial solutions: battery energy storage systems (BESS) -> page ''/'', capabilities, products", "Production and service footprint in North America and Europe -> capabilities, products", "Over 5 GWh production capacity -> products", "Global supply base for cells and components -> products", "Remanufacturing to extend product life -> products", "Full mechanical, electrical, testing, and validation capabilities -> capabilities", "Engineering services -> capabilities", "Removable electronics unit (RCB) for easy service and repair -> capabilities", "Cell-agnostic hardware and software architecture -> products", "Automotive-grade battery technology -> capabilities", "Industries: industrial energy storage, grid interaction, stationary energy storage -> industries_served", "NMC battery technology -> industries_served"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We design and manufacture the systems that define the way the world moves forward.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='borgwarner-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Boston Electronics operates from Brookline, Massachusetts. For forty years it has served as a distributor of electro-optical solutions, though a specific founding year is not disclosed.

The firm distributes advanced electro-optical components and specialized systems for microscopy, offering a broad portfolio that includes UV sensors and probes (SiC photodiodes), UV LEDs (255–405 nm), infrared detectors and imaging arrays (InGaAs PIN/APD, InAsSb, T2SLS), terahertz sources and imagers (QCL-based), photon-counting modules (TCSPC/FLIM), quantum cascade lasers, and laboratory instrumentation such as blackbody sources and laser power meters. It provides knowledgeable application support to help customers select and integrate these technologies.

Customers span environmental monitoring, process control, scientific instrumentation, life sciences and biomedical technologies, building and home automation, security and surveillance, and microscopy. The company works with researchers and manufacturers developing products for water and air purification, curing, lidar, thermal imaging, and spectroscopy.

Boston Electronics positions itself as a specialist in photo-detection and photon generation, representing manufacturers worldwide—including Hamamatsu, Becker & Hickl, Alpes Lasers, and Gentec-EO—to bring advantaged, unique-performance solutions to a broad market. Its stated differentiator is close collaboration with customers to address sensor requirements across diverse applications.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Distribution of advanced electro-optical components", "Application engineering and technical support", "Photo-detection and photon generation expertise", "Photon-counting (TCSPC/FLIM) system support", "UV, IR, and THz sensor integration consulting"], "industries": ["Environmental monitoring", "Process control", "Scientific instrumentation", "Life sciences", "Biomedical technologies", "Building automation", "Home automation", "Security", "Surveillance", "Microscopy"], "materials": ["Silicon Carbide (SiC)", "InGaAs", "InAsSb", "InAs", "T2SLS", "UV LED semiconductors", "IR emitter semiconductors", "Quantum cascade laser materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Knowledgeable application support for sensor selection and integration", "Broad portfolio of advanced electro-optical components from leading global manufacturers", "Specialist expertise in photo-detection and photon generation (UV, IR, THz)", "Longstanding distribution relationships with premier photonics suppliers", "Technical consulting to match solutions to specific application requirements"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Brookline, Massachusetts -> db", "Tradename of 49Chestnut LLC and Fiber Optic Center, Inc. -> /about", "Acquired by Fiber Optic Center, Inc. in November 2025 -> /about", "Forty years as distributor of electro-optical solutions -> /about", "Distributor of advanced electro-optical components and specialized systems for microscopy -> /", "Product portfolio includes UV sensors, UV LEDs, IR detectors, THz sources, photon-counting modules, QCLs, instrumentation -> /", "Markets served: environmental monitoring, process control, scientific instrumentation, life sciences, biomedical technologies, building automation, home automation, security, surveillance, microscopy -> /about", "Specialists in photo-detection and photon generation -> /about", "Partners include Hamamatsu, Becker & Hickl, Alpes Lasers, Gentec-EO, etc. -> /about", "ROHS certification -> db", "Knowledgeable application support -> /, /about", "Web store with product filtering -> /", "Distribution agreement with PremierPhotonics -> /", "THz laser power measurement from Gentec-EO -> /", "Universal Photon Source Driver 2.0 -> /", "VioBeam Ultra Narrow Beam UV LEDs -> /", "Partnership with Hamamatsu for mid-infrared detectors and LEDs -> /", "THz and MMW sources and detectors from Lytid -> /", "Expanded UV SiC high dose resistant photodetectors -> /", "Portable Android-based UV radiometers -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a distributor of advanced electro-optical components and specialized systems for microscopy.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='boston-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Boulder Furniture Arts, a fine furniture design and build studio, has operated from Boulder, Colorado since its founding in 1985.

The firm produces two distinct lines: BFA Classic, a collection of largely unchanged designs dating back to 1985, and BFA Create, a custom arm that develops one-of-a-kind pieces including live-edge tables, built-in cabinetry, and mixed-material installations such as walnut-and-steel podiums or resin river tables. Production follows a 1-person-1-piece fabrication model supported by a 10-year apprenticeship program, with finishing limited to hand-rubbed oils and custom-matched commercial options. The shop also handles delivery, full-service installation, shipping, and a lifetime care program covering repair, refinishing, disassembly, and relocation.

Clients range from architects and interior designers who require precise collaboration to residents and families seeking heirloom-quality furnishings. The company also serves institutional leaders, artists, and environmentally conscious buyers who value carbon-storing materials.

Boulder Furniture Arts distinguishes itself by sourcing all hardwoods within a two-day drive of its shop, guaranteeing every piece for life, and rejecting surplus inventory. The founders frame the business as an “old-school working art house run by people who give a damn,” emphasizing analog modern aesthetics, playful restraint, and a direct maker-to-client relationship.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Live-edge fabrication", "Built-in cabinetry", "Installation services", "Concept development", "Sample and resource library", "Layout and budget planning", "Upholstery specification", "CAD design and renderings", "Interior design collaboration", "1-person-1-piece fabrication", "10-year apprenticeship training", "Zero-surplus production", "Hand-rubbed oil finishing", "Custom finish matching", "Commercial finish options", "Built-and-brought delivery", "Full-service installation", "Shipping coordination", "Furniture repair and refinishing", "Disassembly and relocation services", "Lifetime guarantee program"], "industries": [], "materials": ["American hardwood", "Walnut", "Steel", "Resin", "Fabric", "Leather"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Sourcing of American hardwoods within a 2-day drive of Boulder", "Lifetime guarantee on all furniture", "1-person-1-piece fabrication with a 10-year apprenticeship model", "Hand-rubbed oil finishes and custom finish matching", "Built-and-brought delivery with full-service installation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1985 -> db", "Headquarters Boulder, Colorado -> db", "Fine furniture design and build -> /", "BFA Classic and BFA Create collections -> /", "Custom design, live edge, built-ins, installation -> /", "1-person-1-piece fabrication -> /", "10-year apprenticeship model -> /", "Hand-rubbed oil finishes -> /", "Custom finish matching -> /", "Built-and-brought delivery -> /", "Full-service installation -> /", "Lifetime guarantee -> /", "Sourcing within 2-day drive -> /", "Customer types: architects, designers, residents, families, leaders, artists, scientists, earthlings -> /", "Materials: American hardwood, walnut, steel, resin, fabric, leather -> /", "No surplus production -> /", "Commercial finish options -> /", "Repair, refinish, disassembly, moves -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "IS A FINE FURNITURE DESIGN+BUILD BASED IN BOULDER, CO FOR OVER 40 YEARS.", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='boulder-furniture-arts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Boulder Technologies, LLC operates from Dover, New Hampshire, where it has served the electronics supply chain for over 25 years.

The firm specializes in sourcing and supplying integrated circuits, passive components, and other board-level parts, with a focus on RoHS-compliant inventory. It offers excess inventory management and outright purchase programs for idle stock, providing flexible, value-added services tailored to dynamic market conditions. The company emphasizes its experienced staff and marketing strategies to act as an independent strategic partner.

Its customer base includes electronic manufacturers, contract manufacturers, original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), and telecommunication equipment manufacturers. The company positions itself as a supplier that stands behind every component sold, with safeguards against fraud and counterfeit products.

Boulder Technologies differentiates itself through its commitment to customer-specific needs, aggressive buying of IC and passive component material, and a policy of backing each component against unscrupulous practices.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic component distribution", "Excess inventory management", "Outright purchase of idle inventory", "Value-added services", "RoHS-compliant parts sourcing", "Counterfeit mitigation"], "industries": ["Electronic manufacturers", "Contract manufacturers", "OEMs", "Telecommunication equipment manufacturers"], "materials": ["Integrated circuits (ICs)", "Passive components"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Flexible services adapted to dynamic markets", "Excess inventory management and outright purchase programs", "Over 25 years of combined industry experience", "Independent strategic partner approach", "Component authenticity guarantee against fraud and counterfeits"], "facts_used": ["Location: Dover, NH -> db", "Description: independent board level electronic components distributor -> db", "Certifications: ROHS -> db", "Capabilities: flexible services, excess management, outright buys -> db", "Products: ROHS compliant parts, board level electronic components -> db", "Industries served: electronic manufacturers, contract manufacturers, OEMs, telecommunication equipment manufacturers -> db", "Experience: over 25 years combined experience -> /", "Address: 6 Faraday Drive, Dover, NH 03820 -> /", "Commitment: stands behind each component, safeguards against fraud/counterfeit -> /", "Aggressive buyer of IC/Passive component material -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Boulder Technologies, LLC is an independent board level electronic components distributor", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_li