UPDATE companies SET description='Brooks Molds operates from Elmore, Alabama, where it has been a family-owned and operated business since 1999. The company traces its roots to 1984, when Bobby Brooks joined the mold and prototype department at Mortar Creek Plastics in Elmore. He advanced to shop supervisor and master pattern maker before launching Brooks Molds in 1999. His son Timothy now works alongside him, continuing the family operation.

The shop specializes in tooling and manufacturing molds for the cast polymer industry, serving producers of cultured marble, Tyvarian, and solid surface materials. The product line includes standard and custom bowls, wall panels, vanity tops, shower pans, shower niches, trim molds, and a range of custom patterns. The company maintains a master inventory of patterns and can handle both standard and custom design-and-build projects.

Customers are primarily cast polymer manufacturers and fabricators across the United States. Testimonials reference companies such as Majestic Kitchen & Bath, Micalline LLC, Amarillo Marble, Elite Marble, The Bath Collection, Carstin Brands, Easton Industries, Custom Bath Products, St. Louis Marble Company, Custom Designer Surface, Hall Marble, and BSWB Inc. These clients use Brooks molds in daily production of countertops, bath fixtures, and wall panels.

The company emphasizes durability and long service life, citing heavy-duty bracing systems, immaculate care of master patterns, and the use of what it describes as the industry''s most effective materials. The goal is to reduce downtime from mold repairs and to deliver molds that stay in peak condition for years. Owners Bobby and Timothy Brooks oversee every build, a practice they say ensures consistent quality and custom solutions for unique mold needs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hand layup mold construction", "Custom mold design and engineering", "Standard mold production", "Master pattern creation and maintenance", "Cast polymer mold tooling", "Fiberglass mold fabrication", "Mold bracing and reinforcement systems"], "industries": ["Cast polymer", "Cultured marble", "Solid surface", "Tyvarian", "Kitchen and bath manufacturing"], "materials": ["Fiberglass", "Cast polymer resins", "Composite resins"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["20+ years in the cast polymer mold business", "Heavy-duty bracing systems for structural integrity", "Owners monitor every step of the hand-layup process", "Master patterns maintained for long-term repeatability", "Custom design and build for standard and unique mold challenges"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1999 -> /about", "Family-owned and operated -> /about", "Bobby Brooks founder, started 1984 at Mortar Creek Plastics -> /about", "Location Elmore, Alabama -> db", "Specializes in cast polymer molds (cultured marble, Tyvarian, solid surface) -> /", "Hand layup construction with owner monitoring -> /", "Product categories: bowls, wall panels, vanity tops, shower pans, niches, trim, custom -> /", "Customers: Majestic Kitchen & Bath, Micalline LLC, Amarillo Marble, Elite Marble, The Bath Collection, Carstin Brands, Easton Industries, Custom Bath Products, St. Louis Marble Company, Custom Designer Surface, Hall Marble, BSWB Inc. -> /", "Heavy-duty bracing systems, master pattern care, durable materials -> /", "Materials: fiberglass, cast polymer resins -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in the tooling and manufacturing of molds for the cast polymer industry", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='brooks-molds' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bud & Mary''s Manufacturing Facility is based in Des Moines, Iowa, and was founded in 2005. The company operates medical cannabis dispensaries in Des Moines and Sioux City, serving patients through retail locations.

The company dispenses medical cannabis products including concentrates, vapes, edible tablets, THC dissolvable powder, creams, and tinctures. In January 2025, it launched its first live resin cannabis product for the Iowa medical market. The company also runs a patient rewards and referral program that offers points for successful referrals.

Bud & Mary''s serves medical cannabis patients in Iowa, with qualifying conditions including chronic pain, multiple sclerosis, and other ailments. The Iowa medical cannabis program, established in 2018, allows cannabis-derived THC products produced from in-state plants. The company''s dispensaries provide access to these regulated, third-party tested products.

