UPDATE companies SET description='Burmeister Woodwork Co operates from Hales Corners, Wisconsin, just south of Milwaukee. The business traces its origins to the early 1920s when Marvin Burmeister founded Advance Millwork; the name was changed to Burmeister Woodwork in 1937. It remained in the Burmeister family for three generations—George Burmeister took over in 1964 and added stair fabrication, and his son Russell Burmeister shifted the focus to high‑end custom architectural millwork in 1981. In 2015, John Sprenger, a military veteran, acquired the company and serves as president.

The firm produces architectural millwork for luxury residential and commercial projects, including cabinetry, stairs, moldings, and doors. Its 40,000‑square‑foot manufacturing facility in Hales Corners houses a team of about 60 craftsmen who engineer, fabricate, finish, and install each piece. A branch office in Chicago supports project coordination across the Midwest and nationally. The shop combines traditional hand craftsmanship with modern technology and regularly incorporates custom veneers, exotic wood species, metal, glass, and upholstery into complex, technically demanding projects.

Burmeister serves the luxury residential market—creating millwork for high‑end homes, penthouses, and historic renovations—and the commercial sector, with projects such as a modern bank lobby. Clients include architects, designers, and builders throughout the Midwest and across the United States who bring the company their most challenging custom woodwork requirements.

John Sprenger has said he was drawn to the company because of its culture of craftsmanship and the pursuit of excellence he learned in the military, a philosophy that continues to drive the firm’s focus on uncompromising artisanship and turning bold design ideas into reality.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Architectural millwork", "Cabinetry", "Stair fabrication", "Moldings", "Doors", "Engineering/design", "Fabrication", "Finishing", "Installation", "Custom veneer application", "Exotic wood species machining", "Metal integration", "Glass integration", "Upholstery integration"], "industries": ["Luxury residential", "Commercial construction", "Architectural millwork"], "materials": ["Wood", "Custom veneer", "Exotic wood species", "Metal", "Glass", "Upholstery"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["40,000 sq ft manufacturing facility in Hales Corners, WI", "In-house engineering, fabrication, finishing, and installation", "Branch office in Chicago for regional project management", "Capability to integrate custom veneer, exotic woods, metal, glass, and upholstery", "Expertise in complex projects with demanding technical requirements"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1937 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Hales Corners, Wisconsin -> db, /services", "Employee count 60 -> /about", "Facility size 40,000 sq ft -> /services", "Branch office Chicago -> /services", "Ownership history (Marvin Burmeister, George, Russell, John Sprenger 2015) -> /about", "John Sprenger president, military veteran -> /about", "Processes: cabinetry, stairs, millwork, moldings, doors -> /services, db", "Engineering, fabrication, finishing, installation -> /services", "Materials: custom veneer, exotic wood species, metal, glass, upholstery -> /services", "Industries: luxury residential, commercial -> /services", "Projects: residential and commercial examples -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": 