UPDATE companies SET description='Burton Electronics Manufacturing Services (Burton EMS) is a family-owned contract manufacturer founded in 1978 by Edward Leman and James Treiterer in New Berlin, Wisconsin. The company moved to a larger facility in Minocqua in the early 1980s, then built a 6,500-square-foot plant in Hazelhurst in the early 1990s where it added surface-mount assembly. Operational control passed to Gary Burnett Sr. in 1997, and the business expanded into Ironwood, Michigan, where it now operates two manufacturing facilities totaling over 20,000 square feet. Headquarters remain in Hazelhurst, WI.

Burton provides full-lifecycle electronics manufacturing services including PCB assembly (SMT and through-hole), box build, mechanical assembly, spray coating, design and engineering, new product introduction, product lifecycle management, and design-for-manufacturability reviews using VAYO software with 1,500 design rules. The Ironwood facilities house SMT lines with 3D solder paste inspection, automated optical inspection, selective soldering (Orissa Synchrodex), reflow ovens, and a water wash system. The company specializes in high-mix, low-to-medium volume production, supporting programs from prototype through full-rate production.

Burton serves OEMs in the medical, industrial, motor control, specialized consumer, security, building controls, defense, and professional tool markets. Customers rely on the company for turnkey, engineering-intensive projects that demand high reliability and variable-demand responsiveness.

The company attributes its differentiation to a "people-driven" culture emphasizing direct communication, teamwork, proactive problem-solving, and integrity. Its quality system targets a first-pass yield above 99%, warranty returns below 0.5%, and on-time delivery exceeding 97%, supported by ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016 certifications, Lean manufacturing, and Six Sigma methodologies.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','ESD Control certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB assembly (SMT and through-hole)", "Box build", "Mechanical assembly", "Spray coating", "Design & engineering", "New Product Introduction (NPI)", "Product Lifecycle Management (PLM)", "Product and PCB design", "Component selection assistance", "Burn-in and product validation", "Product documentation", "Component engineering", "Expedited transition to full production", "Incoming inspection and part verification", "Traceability (unique ID per assembly step)", "3D Solder Paste Inspection (SPI)", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "Selective soldering (Orissa Synchrodex)", "Water wash system", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM) with VAYO software", "Program management", "Lean manufacturing (5S, Six Sigma)", "Quality Management System (ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016)", "Lead-free processes", "ESD control"], "industries": ["Medical", "Industrial", "Motor control", "Specialized consumer", "Security", "Building controls", "Defense", "Professional tools"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Water wash system", "Orissa Synchrodex selective solder system", "Placement machines", "Reflow ovens", "Solder paste application equipment", "3-D solder paste inspection machines", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI) machines", "SMT lines"], "volume": "High-mix, low-to-medium volume; prototype to production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["People-driven culture with direct communication and teamwork", "Warranty return rate less than 0.5% of product shipped", "On-time delivery greater than 97%", "First pass yield at final inspection above 99%", "Intelligent DFM review with VAYO software (1,500 design check rules)", "Dedicated program manager with Customer-Focused Team per project"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1978 by Edward Leman and James Treiterer -> /about-us", "Family-owned company -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Hazelhurst, WI -> /about-us", "Two manufacturing plants in Ironwood, MI -> /about-us", "6,500 sq ft facility built in Hazelhurst early 1990s -> /about-us", "Ironwood facility expanded to 20,000 sq ft in 2006/2007 -> /about-us", "Second Ironwood facility acquired 2021-2022 -> /about-us", "SMT lines expanded with new equipment 2022 -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016 certifications -> /quality", "RoHS compliance and ESD Control certified -> /quality", "High-mix, low-to-medium volume specialization -> /about", "Industries served: medical, industrial, motor control, specialized consumer, security, building controls, defense, professional tools -> /about", "People-driven culture description -> /about-us", "Quality objectives: first pass yield >99%, warranty returns <0.5%, on-time delivery >97% -> /quality", "DFM with VAYO software (1500 design rules) -> /quality", "Program manager with Customer-Focused Team -> /quality", "Equipment: water wash, Orissa Synchrodex, placement machines, reflow ovens, solder paste equipment, 3D SPI, AOI -> /about-us", "Capabilities: PCB assembly, box build, mechanical assembly, spray coating, design/engineering, NPI, PLM, component selection, burn-in, documentation, component engineering, expedited production -> /about-us, /quality, db", "Traceability via unique ID per assembly step -> /quality", "Incoming inspection and verification -> /quality", "Lean manufacturing, 5S, Six Sigma -> /quality"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Burton Industries, Inc. provides customized manufacturing solutions to OEMs in the medical, indu