UPDATE companies SET description='Cables & Chips operates from New York City, where it was founded in 1982. The company began by hand‑soldering custom computer cables for local and national retailers, then expanded into structured cabling, voice and data networks, fiber optic systems, and broader low‑voltage infrastructure as technology evolved.

Today the firm designs, installs, organizes, tests, and supports the physical infrastructure behind business networks, WiFi, security, A/V, conference rooms, and server‑room environments. Its services cover structured CAT6 and CAT6a cabling, cable testing and certification, fiber optic installation and termination, VoIP infrastructure, cable cleanup and MDF/IDF organization, server rack installation, WiFi design and access‑point cabling, cellular signal boosters, conference‑room AV, CCTV and access‑control cabling, and PA/audio‑visual systems.

Clients include commercial offices, secure facilities, server rooms, and building‑upgrade projects across New York City. Concrete examples from the company’s project list include a corporate headquarters full network infrastructure, a data‑center retrofit and rack cleanup, a financial‑services WiFi and security upgrade, and a conference‑room AV boardroom upgrade. The firm also provides field support for IT consultants, managed service providers, contractors, and internal technology teams.

