cture behind business networks, fiber, WiFi, security systems, A/V, conference rooms, and commercial technology environments.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cables-and-chips' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cadillac Products Automotive Company, headquartered in Troy, Michigan, traces its roots to 1942 when M.P. Williams, a partner in the Cadillac Bookbinding Company, founded Cadillac Bag Company to fulfill a defense packaging program for Chrysler during World War II. The business remains fourth-generation family-owned and managed, with the Williams family still directing operations across multiple Michigan facilities and a plant in Schertz, Texas.

The company converts plastics into protective, acoustical, and water-shield components for vehicle interiors, exteriors, and underbody applications. Its integrated manufacturing includes cast and blown film extrusion, robotic adhesive dispensing, in-house prototyping, custom injection molding, automated assembly, thermoforming and cold forming, die and water-jet cutting, and a certified test laboratory. Proprietary product lines such as SOUNDLOC™ acoustic barriers and FIBERSORB™ fiber mats are produced across facilities that together employ roughly 225 people and generate annual sales exceeding $50 million.

Programs have covered door watershields, dash mats, transmission shields, wheel liners, and energy-absorption bumper systems. During the COVID-19 pandemic the company also applied its converting expertise to medical gown production.

Founded to meet urgent wartime needs, Cadillac Products emphasizes full vertical integration under one roof, 100% U.S.-based production, and rapid prototyping that can verify concepts in days. The family ownership model is cited as a driver of long-term customer dedication and operational continuity.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16949:2016','ISO 14001:2015','ISO 45001:2018']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cast film extrusion", "Blown film extrusion", "Robotic adhesive application", "In-house prototyping and design", "Custom injection molding", "Automated assembly (pads, fibers, foams to substrates)", "Thermoforming", "Cold forming", "Steel rule die cutting", "Water jet cutting (robotic)", "In-house testing laboratory", "FIBERSORB\u2122 AC (thermoset resin impregnated fiber mat)", "FIBERSORB\u2122 WL (synthetic shoddy fiber mat for wheel liners)", "Molded fiber (PET or shoddy fibers)", "FIBERSORB\u2122 ACB (<130\u00b0C synthetic shoddy fiber mat)", "SOUNDLOC\u2122 (filled EVA acoustic resin)", "Die cutting (flat PET, PP, cotton shoddy fiber)", "FIBERSORB\u2122 GL (thermoset impregnated mat with glass fiber)", "SOUNDLOC-Seal\u2122 (EVA barrier with fiber decoupler, patented seal technology)", "Thin wall hybrid molding (variable thickness injection molding)", "FIBERSORB\u2122 NF (impregnated mat with natural fibers)", "CONTROL FLOW-SL (dissipative multi-layer hard shell acoustical product)", "Polyethylene barrier (air, dust, moisture barrier)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Medical"], "materials": ["Plastic resin pellets", "Polyethylene", "EVA (ethylene vinyl acetate)", "Thermoset resin", "Cotton shoddy fiber", "Synthetic shoddy fiber", "PET (polyethylene terephthalate)", "Polypropylene (PP)", "Glass fiber", "Natural fibers", "Adhesives"], "equipment": ["Polyethylene cast film extruder", "Injection molding machines", "Robotic adhesive dispensing systems", "Water jet cutting robots", "Automation robotics", "In-house testing laboratory equipment"], "volume": "", "