UPDATE companies SET description='Calgreg Electronics operates from Warwick, Rhode Island, where founder Robert Mazzeo established the business to address a gap he saw in the electronics supply chain. Mazzeo recognized that manufacturers needed more than just component delivery—they required rapid engineering support, inventory management, and a suite of value-added services from a single distribution partner.

The company distributes a broad line of electronic and electromechanical components—interconnects, thermal management products, wedge-loks, rugged card guides, enclosures, and enclosure hardware—while also providing in-house design, testing, and assembly services.

The firm’s vendor-managed inventory and design capabilities are aimed at customers looking to reduce procurement overhead and accelerate product development cycles.

The company’s differentiation rests on combining distribution with technical services that are typically sourced separately. By integrating design, test, and thermal analysis under one roof, Calgreg aims to give customers “tactically quick” engineering support while managing inventory risk through its Asian supply network. and global divisions.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electromechanical component distribution", "Electronic packaging product distribution", "Value-added assembly", "Design services (electrical and mechanical)", "Electrical testing", "Thermal management design and testing", "Vendor Managed Inventory (VMI)", "Supply chain management with Asian suppliers"], "industries": ["Electronics"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vendor Managed Inventory (VMI) programs", "Electrical and mechanical design services", "Thermal management design and testing", "Supply management with Asian supplier network"], "facts_used": ["Distributor of electronic and electromechanical components -> /", "Value-added services including design, testing, and assembly -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified (USA and Global) -> /", "Founder Robert Mazzeo -> /about", "Vendor Managed Inventory (VMI) -> /about", "Electrical and mechanical design services -> /about", "Thermal management design and testing -> /about", "Supply management with Asian supplier network -> /about", "Headquarters Warwick, Rhode Island -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "value-added services including design, testing, and assembly", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='calgreg-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cali-Fabworks was founded in 2001 in Anaheim, California, and operates from a facility on East Miraloma Avenue. The company is led by CEO Bryan Rios and focuses on architectural metal fabrication for both residential and commercial clients.

The shop produces custom gates, steel and glass doors, railings, bar cabinets, shelving, fireplace doors, and other bespoke metalwork. Its in-house process covers design, fabrication, powder coating with baked zinc primer, metallization, and installation. The company serves Orange County and surrounding cities including Newport, Laguna, Orange, Tustin, and Irvine.

Customers range from homeowners seeking custom entry gates and interior railings to businesses needing storefront doors, office partitions, and commercial stair railings. Recent projects include exterior entry doors, sliding and French doors, pivot doors, and aluminum gates for rust protection.

