UPDATE companies SET description='Cameron Manufacturing & Design operates from two facilities: a 145,000-square-foot plant in Horseheads, New York, and a 28,000-square-foot operation in Orlando, Florida. The company was founded in 1983 by Frank LaViola Sr. to address a regional need for custom fabrication in upstate New York. In 2007, LaViola transitioned the business to an Employee Stock Ownership Plan (ESOP), making the workforce the company''s owners.

The firm provides custom metal manufacturing across the full project lifecycle — engineering design, CNC machining (milling, lathing, waterjet and laser cutting), sheet metal fabrication (rolling, bending, punching), heavy and sanitary welding with CWI oversight, in-house finishing (powder coating, painting, vibratory tumbling), and on-site installation with documentation packages. The combined facilities employ hundreds of skilled workers.

Cameron serves food and dairy processors requiring USDA- and 3A-compliant equipment, rail and transit agencies needing custom metal components and signaling systems, and a mix of Fortune 500 and regional manufacturers seeking turnkey process equipment.

LaViola started the business as a local "fab shop" focused on quality workmanship, on-time delivery, and customer service. The ESOP structure was adopted to preserve that culture by vesting ownership in the employees who execute the work, a model the company credits for its ability to adapt across decades of industry change.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001','USDA compliant','3A Industrial Standards compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC machining", "CNC milling", "CNC lathing", "Waterjet cutting", "Laser cutting", "Custom sheet metal fabrication", "Rolling", "Bending", "Punching", "Heavy fabrication", "Welding (CWI certified)", "Sanitary welding", "Powder coating", "Painting", "Vibratory tumbling", "Engineering design services", "Project management", "Equipment installation", "Turnkey systems integration", "2D/3D CAD design", "Custom machinery building", "Metal finishing services", "Contract engineering services", "On-site installation and start-up support"], "industries": ["Food & Dairy", "Beverage", "Rail & Transit", "Industrial Manufacturing"], "materials": ["Carbon steel", "Stainless steel", "Inconel", "Monel", "Hastelloy", "Nickel"], "equipment": ["Amada Punch/Laser LC-2012 C1 NT", "Amada Fiber laser", "Laser cutting equipment", "Waterjet cutting equipment", "Forming equipment", "Welders", "Powder coating equipment", "Painting equipment", "Vibratory tumbler"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned (ESOP) since 2007", "ISO 9001 & ISO 14001 certified at Horseheads, NY facility", "USDA and 3A compliant for food, beverage, and dairy equipment", "Turnkey capability: design, fabrication, machining, welding, finishing, and installation under one roof"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1983 by Frank LaViola Sr. -> /about-us", "Employee-owned (ESOP) since 2007 -> /about-us", "Two locations: Horseheads, NY (145,000 sq ft) and Orlando, FL (28,000 sq ft) -> /about-us", "Hundreds of skilled employees -> /about-us", 