UPDATE companies SET description='Carson Manufacturing Inc. is a family-owned manufacturer of planetary gearheads based in Carson City, Nevada. The company traces its roots to 1986, when Eddie Capps and his wife Barbara purchased the business. Three generations of the family have since guided the operation, including their daughter Delores Stacy, now vice president, and her son Kenny Penn, a sales engineer. A pivotal redesign in 1996 introduced a bearing-holder architecture that aligns gears along the centerline, a method that later became an industry standard.

The company produces several gearhead lines — Precision, Eliminator, “S” Series, and Right Angle (RE and RP) — covering sizes 17 through 56 and standard ratios from 3:1 to 100:1, with custom ratios up to 10,000:1. It maintains over 231 standard models and operates an internal research and development division where every design undergoes strenuous testing under multiple conditions. Custom gearheads are engineered to mount virtually any motor, and the company does not charge a design fee for custom work.

Customers span medical device makers (including cancer-detection equipment), paper-production machinery, motion-control and robotics integrators, aerospace programs such as Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University, HVAC manufacturers, and supply-chain automation firms like Attabotics. The company also serves servo-system distributors and industrial OEMs.

Carson Manufacturing emphasizes on-time, on-budget delivery, with standard units shipping in two days and custom designs completed in a week. All products are made entirely in the United States, avoiding tariffs and reducing shipping costs. The firm’s differentiators include the no-fee custom design policy, the 1996 bearing-holder innovation, and a testing regimen that validates each configuration before shipment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Planetary gearhead design", "Custom gearhead engineering", "Precision machining", "Assembly", "Strenuous testing under multiple conditions", "Research and development", "No-charge custom design service", "Standard gearhead production (231+ models)", "Right-angle gearhead manufacturing", "High-ratio gearheads (up to 10,000:1)", "IP65 and IP54 enclosure rating compliance"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Paper production", "Motion control", "Robotics", "Aerospace", "HVAC", "Supply chain automation", "Servo systems", "Industrial automation"], "materials": ["Hard-anodized aluminum", "Alloy steel", "Stainless steel", "Hardened steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Standard products ship within 2 days; custom designs with set parameters completed in a week", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No design fee for custom gearheads", "Standard gearheads ship in 2 days", "Custom designs with set parameters completed in a week", "100% manufactured in the USA (tariff-free)", "Internal R&D division with strenuous testing of every design"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 -> db", "Headquarters Carson City, Nevada -> db", "Family-owned, purchased by Eddie Capps and Barbara -> /about-us", "Three generations: Delores Stacy (VP), Kenny Penn (sales engineer) -> /about-us", "1996 bearing-holder redesign -> /about-us", "Product lines: Precision, Eliminator, S Series, Right Angle RE/RP -> /about-us", "Sizes 17-56, ratios 3:1-100:1 standard, up to 10,000:1 custom -> /about-us", "231+ standard models -> /", "Internal R&D division, strenuous testing -> /about-us", "No design fee for custom gearheads -> /about-us", "Standard ship in 2 days, custom in a week -> /", "100% USA made, tariff-free -> /", "Industries: medical (cancer detection), paper production, motion control, robotics, aerospace (Embry-Riddle), HVAC (MAS HVAC), supply chain automation (Attabotics), servo systems (Servo Systems Co.) -> /about-us, /", "Materials: hard-anodized brackets, alloy steel ring gear, stainless steel output shaft, hardened steel gears -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "After 48 years of operations, the company is well-known, a leading manufacturer of planetary gearheads.", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='carson-manufacturing-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cascade Systems Technology, based in Hillsboro, Oregon, has served as a supplier of choice for electronic manufacturing services for more than 36 years. The company operates as a domestic contract manufacturer without publicly disclosed ownership structure or founder details.

The firm provides a full spectrum of electronic assembly processes, including surface mount technology with BGA and micro BGA placement, through-hole, press-fit, microelectronics assembly, board de-panelization, conformal coating (acrylic, silicone, polyurethane), box build integration, cable and wire harness assembly, design for testability and manufacturing, and rework services. Its capabilities span PCB assembly, mechanical assembly, and functional testing, though facility size, headcount, and annual volume figures are not disclosed.

CST serves industries such as aerospace and defense, medical devices, semiconductor manufacturing, clean energy and EV battery storage, sensors and instrumentation, industrial controls, and emerging AI/data center/quantum computing sectors. Customer references include a semiconductor manufacturer, a clean energy/EV power supply manufacturer, a semiconductor company, and a semiconductor fab infrastructure manufacturer.

